# TradingView VWAP Breakout Retest Trend

## Source
- Source: [[sources/tradingview-mechanical-strategy-scripts]]
- Page / Timestamp: TradingView script `VWAP Breakout Retest Trend Strategy`, author handle `AIScripts`, open-source strategy, page shows 2026-03-09, accessed 2026-05-22, https://www.tradingview.com/script/zYIRkvHS-VWAP-Breakout-Retest-Trend-Strategy/

## Mechanics

### Entry
Use M15/M30 intraday baseline. Compute session VWAP, trend EMA, and ATR.

- Long setup:
  - Price crosses above VWAP.
  - Price later pulls back toward VWAP within the configured retest buffer.
  - Price remains above trend EMA.
  - Enter on bullish confirmation after the retest.
- Short setup:
  - Price crosses below VWAP.
  - Price later pulls back toward VWAP from below within the configured retest buffer.
  - Price remains below trend EMA.
  - Enter on bearish confirmation after the retest.

### Exit
- Exit at ATR-based stop-loss or ATR-based take-profit.
- Optional signal exit: close if price crosses back through VWAP against the position before target.

### Stop Loss
Source uses ATR-based dynamic risk management. V5 baseline: stop = 1.5 * ATR(14), target = 2.5 * ATR(14), with P3 sweep.

### Position Sizing
V5 default: fixed-risk $1,000 for P2 baseline, one position per symbol/magic.

### Zusatzliche Filter
- VWAP must be session-anchored and available for at least 8 bars.
- Retest buffer defaults to 0.25 * ATR(14) around VWAP.
- Confirmation candle defaults to close in breakout direction after retest.

## Concepts (what kind of strategy is this)
- [[concepts/vwap-breakout]] - initial cross away from session fair value defines directional interest.
- [[concepts/retest-confirmation]] - waits for VWAP to hold as support/resistance.
- [[concepts/trend-filter-ma]] - EMA trend alignment suppresses counter-trend retests.

